<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 23 April, from 1014 to 1985.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brian-boru.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1014">1014 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,012 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brian Boru wins at Clontarf but is killed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Irish high king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> defeated the forces of Leinster and their Norse allies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and beyond. He was slain in his tent during the battle, and his hard-won supremacy collapsed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1348">1348 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">678 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Order of the Garter is founded, by tradition on St George's Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward III created the Order of the Garter, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s senior order of chivalry, around this time, traditionally marked on St George's Day. Its 24 knights still meet at Windsor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Shakespeare is born, by tradition, in Stratford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shakespeare's birth is traditionally dated to 23 April; only his baptism on 26 April is recorded. He went on to write some 38 plays and 154 sonnets.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1616">1616 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">410 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Shakespeare dies in Stratford-upon-Avon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shakespeare died at his home of New Place, aged 52. Seven years later his fellow actors gathered 36 of his plays in the First Folio, preserving many that might otherwise have been lost.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Future president James Buchanan is born</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Buchanan was born in a log cabin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. The 15th US president, and the only one never to marry, failed to halt the secession of Southern states in 1860 and 1861.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1985">1985 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">41 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coca-Cola launches New Coke</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Coca-Cola replaced its 99-year-old formula with a sweeter recipe. Public protest was so strong that the original returned as Coca-Cola Classic 79 days later.</p></div></li></ol>
